# SyncSenta — Implementation Reference

*AI-readable knowledge document. Read before starting any session on this repo.
For the domain glossary, read CONTEXT.md first.*

---

## What SyncSenta is

SyncSenta (`studio/`) is an AI-powered Kenyan K–9 education platform delivering
adaptive learning aligned with Kenya's Competency-Based Curriculum (CBC).

**Core value proposition:**
- Students (PP1–Grade 9): Adaptive Socratic tutor with Omega decision engine,
  interactive CBC activities, XP progression, cross-device continuity
- Teachers: Real-time analytics, misconception detection, CBC content generators
  (schemes, lesson plans, assessments), intervention tools

**Deployed at:** sentastudio.vercel.app  
**Repository:** dgithinjibit/Ascendra (monorepo)

---

## Current stack (September 2026)

```
Frontend:    Next.js 16 · React 18 · TypeScript · Tailwind CSS · shadcn/ui
Auth + DB:   Supabase (Postgres · RLS · Realtime · Storage)
LLM:         Groq llama-3.3-70b-versatile (switchable to Gemini via LLM_PROVIDER env)
Session:     Upstash Redis — LearningSession per user, 7-day TTL
AI backend:  FastAPI (Python 3.11) on Render — LangGraph orchestrator, CBC generators
Adaptive:    TypeScript (active): lib/omega-agent/metta-core.ts
             Rust (source of truth, built, not deployed): rust-core/src/agent_runtime.rs
Deploy:      Vercel (Studio) + Render (AI Agents)
```

---

## Monorepo structure

```
studio/          Next.js 16 — primary web application (THE main codebase)
ai-agents/       FastAPI — LangGraph, teacher generators (schemes, lessons, assessments)
rust-core/       Rust library — adaptive tutoring decision engine (source of truth)
rust-service/    Rust HTTP service wrapping rust-core (built, not yet deployed)
scheme-scribe/   Standalone Vite/React — separate Supabase project (independent)
arduino/         ESP32-CAM firmware prototype (not connected to production)
supabase/        Database migrations (source of truth)
docs/            Architecture, development, and reference documentation
CONTEXT.md       Domain glossary — read first in every session
CODING_STANDARDS.md  Studio coding conventions
```

**Deleted in cleanup (September 2026):**
